---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";

const title = "About This FERS Retirement Calculator Project";
const description =
  "Independent, free FERS retirement calculator built for US federal employees. Learn who we are, how the estimates work, and the sources behind every formula.";
const updated = "2026-09-10";

const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "AboutPage",
  name: title,
  description: description,
  url: "https://www.fers-retirement-calculator.com/about/",
  inLanguage: "en",
  dateModified: updated,
};
---

<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical="https://www.fers-retirement-calculator.com/about/"
  schema={schema}
  updatedTime={updated}
>
  <section class="hero-sheen border-b border-line bg-surface">
    <div class="page-shell py-14 sm:py-16">
      <p class="text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-accent">About</p>
      <h1 class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-balance text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-5xl">
        About FERS Retirement Calculator
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted">
        A free, independent estimator that helps US federal employees understand their FERS pension before making a retirement decision.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-pad">
    <div class="page-shell max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">Why we built this calculator</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Federal employees face a high-stakes decision: when to retire, which retirement type to choose, and how survivor benefits
        change the math. Official tools exist, but few explain the rules behind the numbers. This project pairs a working
        calculator with plain-English explanations of High-3, MRA+10, the FERS Supplement, COLA, and deferred versus postponed
        retirement, so you can see both the estimate and the reasoning.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">How the estimates work</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
        The calculator runs entirely in your browser using the standard FERS formula: your High-3 average salary multiplied by
        years of creditable service and a 1% multiplier, rising to 1.1% if you retire at age 62 or later with at least 20 years of
        service. Advanced inputs cover unused sick leave (converted at 2,087 hours per year), military buyback deposits, special
        category multipliers for law enforcement officers, firefighters, and air traffic controllers, and survivor benefit
        elections. The FERS Supplement is approximated from your projected Social Security benefit at age 62, scaled by your FERS
        service divided by 40.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
        These rules come from OPM's FERS computation guidance and the underlying statute. The formulas and multipliers are checked
        by hand against worked examples before every release.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">Editorial standards</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Content is reviewed against OPM's FERS Computation guidance at least once a year, and the review date is updated whenever
        material changes are made — the latest review is shown in the page metadata. Corrections are welcome: if you find a
        formula or rule that does not match official guidance, contact us and we will verify and fix it.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">Independence and funding</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
        This site is independently operated and completely free. There are no accounts, no paywalls, and no data collection from
        the calculator itself — your inputs never leave your browser. The site is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected
        to the US Office of Personnel Management or any government agency. For official benefit determinations, always work with
        your agency HR office and OPM.
      </p>

      <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-3xl">Contact</h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-muted">
        Questions, corrections, or feedback? Email
        <a href="mailto:hello@fers-retirement-calculator.com" class="font-semibold text-primary hover:underline">hello@fers-retirement-calculator.com</a>
        or visit the <a href="/contact/" class="font-semibold text-primary hover:underline">contact page</a>. You can also read our
        <a href="/privacy/" class="font-semibold text-primary hover:underline">privacy policy</a> and
        <a href="/terms/" class="font-semibold text-primary hover:underline">terms of use</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
